==Norwegian Nynorsk==

===Etymology 1===
{{wikipedia|lang=nn}}
[[File:Toes.jpg|thumb|'''tå''', a toe on a human foot]]
{{root|nn|ine-pro|*deyḱ-}}
From {{inh|nn|non|tá}}, from {{inh|nn|gem-pro|*taihwǭ}}. from the {{der|nn|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*deyḱ-||to point out}}. Cognate with {{cog|la|digitus}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|nn|Taa|taa||obsolete spellings}}

====Noun====
{{nn-noun-irreg|f|tåa|tær|tærne}}

# {{senseid|nn|toe}} a [[toe]] {{q|part of a foot; also part of a sock, stocking or shoe}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nn|frå topp til tå}}
* {{l|nn|litletå}}
* {{l|nn|stortå}}
* {{l|nn|tåfis}}
* {{l|nn|vesletå}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|nn|non|þá}}, from {{der|nn|gem-pro|*þawō}}. Related to the verb {{m|nn|tø}} (from {{der|nn|non|þeyja}}). Related to {{cog|en|thaw}}.

====Noun====
{{nn-noun-f1}}

# {{senseid|nn|thawed ground}} [[thaw]]ed [[ground]]; ground that is free from [[frost]] and [[ice]]

====Adjective====
{{head|nn|adjective|neuter singular|tått|definite singular and plural|tå|or|tåe|comparative|tåare|indefinite superlative|tåast|definite superlative|tåaste}}

# [[thaw]]ed, [[bare]], free of [[ice]] and [[frost]]
#: {{syn|nn|berr|telefri}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nn|tåe}}
* {{l|nn|tåen}}

===Etymology 3===
There is a suspected relation to {{m|nn|tæ}} and {{m|nn|teia}}, from {{der|nn|gmq-pro|ᛏᚨᚹᛁᛞᛟ|gloss=I made}}, from {{der|nn|gem-pro|*tawjaną}}.

====Verb====
{{nn-verb-3}}

# {{lb|nn|transitive}} to [[pick]] apart, [[dissolve]]

===Etymology 4===
Aasen, in his 1850 dictionary, lists it as a variant of {{m|nn|ut av}}.<ref>{{R:Aasen1850|taa}}</ref><ref>{{R:Aasen1850|ut-av}}</ref> As such, the origin of this word is not too dissimilar from that of {{m|nn|på||on}} from Old Norse {{m|nn|upp á}}. See also {{m|nn|tu}} and {{m|nn|poinni}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|nn|ta||the same etymology}}
* {{alt|nn|taa||obsolete spelling}}

